\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.48}{\ignorespaces Absolute (top row) and normalised (bottom row) differential cross-section measurement as a function of the \ensuremath  {p_{\text  {T}}}\xspace  of the leading jet which is not associated with the \ensuremath  {WbWb}\xspace  system compared to interference generators (left column) and other MC generators (right column). The \ensuremath  {t\bar  {t}}\xspace  prediction used here was reweighted to increase the agreement of the top-quark kinematics between data and measurement. The cross-section is unfolded at particle-level in the fiducial phase-space. The unfolded data are shown as black points, while coloured points indicate the MC predictions. Data points are placed at the centre of each bin while predictions are shifted for clarity. Uncertainties are shown by the shaded bands. The lower panel shows the ratio of the MC predictions to the unfolded data.}}{55}{figure.caption.147}\protected@file@percent }
